From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:43:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] flash: a plugin frame without the wait, and a way straight to
 the card (T-576)

Bloxorz (36 fps) ran at 12 frames a second on the GPU path, against the stock browser's 28.6. Timed per frame:
Flash's own work 27 ms, its draw 2 ms, the synchronous Show 14-17 ms, nearly all of it waiting for the daemon's
main thread; and four copies on the parent's side.

- JihadShow/JihadShowDone: Show without the wait. Two surfaces take turns, so at most two frames are in flight
  and a draw due with two out waits for the answer without blocking the player.
- The glib pump is the player's clock and its delay started when a frame's work ended: 16 ms after 20 ms of work
  capped a movie at 27 frames a second. 4 ms while a movie plays, and it stops at a posted draw, or the player ran
  its next frame with this one never drawn.
- An opaque source keeps an opaque format: as B8G8R8A8 with its alpha forced the frame was blended over a white fill.
- A floor of 28 ms between draws. Bubble Tanks at 55 fps had each frame drawn and copied 50 times a second, and the
  card fell to 24 where the stock browser holds 32.
- jihad_plugin_lane_copy, _proof, _set: the frame for the daemon's plugin lane, the display-list proof that nothing
  lies over the plugin, and the plugin's marks off while the lane is open, so that the compositor's count of
  requests means the page changed. jihad_offscreen_compositor_animating says an animation wants frames.

The timers of a frame's parts are in the 2 s readouts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
